Why this is fast

#pragma omp parallel creates the worker team only once, avoiding repeated thread creation overhead across reps.

schedule(static) divides the array into approximately equal-sized contiguous chunks, minimizing scheduling overhead and improving cache locality.

Each thread updates independent elements of y, so there are no race conditions.

The implicit barrier at the end of each omp for ensures each repetition finishes before the next begins, preserving the original dependency between repetitions.

This works correctly for OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 through 10.

The computation remains memory-bound, so static scheduling and minimal synchronization are the best choices here.

